-- and the second: the exchange composed with the reflection — which reverses every arrangement, taking
-- (a,b,c) to (a,c,b), so that the pair of hydrogens exchanged and then reflected reads (h2, cs, h1) — is
-- a rotation of the original, by the path the type carries. So in a medium that admits reflections the
-- two positions are one again: they are enantiotopic, and the medium and not the molecule decides which
-- verdict holds. Three groups, three verdicts, one molecule.
cyc-mirror-swap-same : cyc nb-h2 nb-cs nb-h1 ≡ cyc nb-h1 nb-h2 nb-cs
cyc-mirror-swap-same = sym (λ i → cyc-rot nb-h1 nb-h2 nb-cs i)
